# `Math.max(...list)` stands in tail position. Whatever the list holds, the built-in comes back to its caller, so the frame may stay and the elements are folded in place, in a loop for each storage.
# A list too long for the stack goes to the call, which refuses it, and so does a list with a hole or with something else than numbers.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="largest" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[list]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[storage]] = Load(b@[[list]], {{*}}Reads:JSArray_butterfly)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[length]] = Load(b@[[storage]], {{*}}Reads:Butterfly_publicLength)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[fits]] = Below(b@{{*}}, $65536(b@{{*}}))
# CHECK: Branch(b@[[fits]], Terminal)
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#
# CHECK: Reads:indexedInt32Properties)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# NONE-LABEL: name="largest" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: :CallList)
# NONE-NOT: :Builtin)
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# IR-LABEL: name="largest"
# IR: TryCallInline -, v0 inlineBuiltin=MathMaxOfArray {{*}} -> done b1(), miss b2()
# IR: b2() frequency=Rare:
# IR-NEXT: = CallBuiltin -, v0 overload=MathMax/0 builtinCallForm=List
